[38;5;252m[1m## Three findings worth your attention[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mThe C [38;5;10m.so[0m doesn't link libm.[22m [38;5;10mc_src/CMakeLists.txt[0m has no [38;5;10mtarget_link_libraries[0m, so [38;5;10msqrtf[0m is left undefined and resolved from the process's global scope. Tests that happened to use [38;5;10msin[0m/[38;5;10mcos[0m worked; others crashed with [38;5;10msymbol lookup error[0m. Handled test-side by pre-loading libm with [38;5;10mRTLD_GLOBAL[0m. [38;5;10mc_src[0m untouched.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mNaN sign selection cannot be matched, and shouldn't be.[22m When two NaN operands meet in a commutative [38;5;10m+[0m/[38;5;10m*[0m, gcc and LLVM keep different ones. This is not a translation defect: gcc isn't even internally consistent ([38;5;10mc2Add[0m's [38;5;10maddss[0m destination holds [38;5;10mb[0m, [38;5;10mc2Dot[0m's [38;5;10mmulss[0m holds [38;5;10ma[0m), and LLVM canonicalizes commutative operand order — I confirmed this by writing [38;5;10mb + a[0m and [38;5;10ma + b[0m as two separate functions and watching LLVM identical-code-fold them into one symbol. IEEE 754 §6.2 leaves the sign unspecified. Comparison is bit-exact everywhere else, including NaN-vs-number, which stays a hard failure.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m[38;5;10mc2GJK[0m with an out-of-range [38;5;10mC2_TYPE[0m reads uninitialized stack.[22m [38;5;10mc2MakeProxy[0m's switch has no [38;5;10mdefault:[0m label, so [38;5;10mc2Proxy pA[0m — an uninitialized local — is never written, and every later read is stack residue. Demonstrated: the identical call [38;5;10mc2GJK(shape, typeA=3, …)[0m returns [38;5;10m0.0[0m after a small-coordinate call and [38;5;10m12727922000.0[0m after a large-coordinate one. There is nothing for the Rust to match. The [3mdeterministic[23m out-of-range-enum paths, [38;5;10mc2Collided[0m and [38;5;10mc2MakeProxy[0m itself, are covered bit-exactly across [38;5;10mi32::MIN[0m/[38;5;10mMAX[0m and one-past-boundary values.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
I also had a wrong assumption caught by my own test: I reasoned [38;5;10miter[0m in the GJK loop could never exceed 2, but [38;5;10mc22[0m/[38;5;10mc23[0m can [3mreduce[23m [38;5;10ms.count[0m, letting the loop append-then-collapse repeatedly. Measured maximum over 1.5M wild inputs is 6. This matters because the [38;5;10miter == 20[0m cap firing is the only path that would leave [38;5;10mverts[count-1].u[0m unwritten in the C; it is not reachable in practice, though I've recorded that as a measurement rather than a proof.[0m[0m
